{
  "header": [
    "ECP-R7 — each entity in a received envelope's `included` map is hash-validated individually.",
    "",
    "Batch 3. The floor row is \"Envelope structure with per-entity hash validation (§3.1)\" and it",
    "BUNDLES: the structure half carries a producer-side MUST (\"The content_hash MUST match the map key\")",
    "that fails independently of receipt validation. Filed as ECP-R7-pending-b; routed (F27), not split.",
    "",
    "SPLIT AND RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-16 against 0.8.2.25 — the SECOND file through ADR-0003, after",
    "ECP-R57. The arms, preconditions and surface that used to live here are now a suite-authored ITEM",
    "(suites/py-prototype/items/entity-core-protocol/ECP-R7-P1.diag). This file states the obligation.",
    "",
    "⛔ WHY THIS FILE MOVED TWICE AND THE INSTRUMENT MOVED NEITHER TIME — READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING ANY",
    "PRIOR ECP-R7 NUMBER. 0.8.2.24 pinned the refusal code and this file was re-authored to say so on",
    "2026-09-14. `suites/py-prototype/prototype/checks.py::check_r7` went on scoring `_refused_any` —",
    "a helper whose own docstring says it is \"for rows that require REJECTION and PIN NO CODE\" — until",
    "2026-09-16. So for two days the file asserted a pinned code, the suite accepted any refusal, and",
    "`make check` was green, `IMPLEMENTS` still named ECP-R7, and the executed-by-a-suite ratchet still",
    "counted it. Every one of those measures a DECLARATION. See AP-18.",
    "",
    "⭐ AND THE PREDICTION COULD NOT HAVE FIRED. This file predicts that peers PASSing under .21 FAIL",
    "under the pin with no peer having changed a line. The instrument passed every peer the prediction",
    "is about, because any refusal satisfied it. A prediction whose instrument cannot falsify it is not",
    "a prediction — it is a sentence. That is the charter's own negative-control rule, pointed at a",
    "prediction instead of at an arm, and nothing in this tree was looking there.",
    "",
    "Read range for this re-authoring: §3.1 whole, §1.8 whole, §4.11 whole, §5.2a whole, §6.5, §9.1's row."
  ],
  "id": "ECP-R7",
  "id_status": "allocated",
  "title": "A received envelope carrying an included entity whose content_hash does not match its {type, data} is refused with a coded 400 hash_mismatch response",
  "spec": "ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL §3.1 (Wire transport optimization)",
  "spec_also": [
    "§1.8 item 1 (both halves: self-consistency AND resolution integrity, 0.8.2.23)",
    "§4.11 (Pre-admission refusals — the NORMATIVE HOME of the refusal-emission obligation, 0.8.2.25)",
    "§4.11's cause/code table, row 3 (resolution integrity -> 400 hash_mismatch, stated at §5.2a)",
    "§5.2a corollary 1 (the decode-boundary code, 0.8.2.24; re-scoped 0.8.2.25)",
    "§6.5 dispatch chain ('Validate each included entity hash')",
    "ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §5.4 (what `non_canonical_ecf` is FOR)",
    "§4.7 (the connection-error registry — and it has no row for this)",
    "§9.1 ('Envelope structure with per-entity hash validation (§3.1)' — the floor row this id binds)",
    "§9 CORE-PREADMISSION-REFUSAL-1 arm (d) (the conformance item, 0.8.2.25 — we do NOT author it)"
  ],
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.26",
  "level": "MUST",
  "level_basis": "keyword",
  "profile": [
    "core"
  ],
  "status": "draft",
  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F24, F27, F64, F76",
  "ruled": "CQ-34 and CQ-35 RULED and folded as §4.11 (0.8.2.25) — the three `inconclusive` arms this file carried are now scored, and the drop and the bare close are DISTINCT failures",
  "reading": [
    "§3.1, BYTE-IDENTICAL AT .24 AND .25 (verified by extracting the section from both snapshots and",
    "comparing): \"On the wire, implementations **MUST** validate each included entity's content_hash",
    "individually per entity fidelity (§1.8). Implementations are **NOT REQUIRED** to compute or validate",
    "the envelope's own content_hash during transport.\" §6.5 orders it: \"Validate root entity hash /",
    "Validate each included entity hash / Root is EXECUTE? ...\". ⇒ THE OBLIGATION IS UNCHANGED. What",
    "moved at .25 is the REFUSAL SHAPE, and only that.",
    "",
    "\"EACH\" IS THE WORD THE PROBE IS BUILT ON. The row does not say \"each included entity the handler",
    "uses\". A peer that validates only the entities it reads (the signature, the capability) satisfies a",
    "weaker rule. So the probe includes an entity the hello has no use for — a well-formed",
    "`primitive/any` entity — and corrupts only that one. §3.1's \"Protocol scope\" paragraph says what",
    "`included` is FOR; it does not relax the validation MUST, and a suite MUST NOT read it as doing so.",
    "",
    "THE ENVELOPE'S OWN HASH IS EXEMPT and nothing here touches it: §3.1's NOT REQUIRED.",
    "",
    "ROOT VALID, PARAMS VALID — so the refusal is attributable to the included entity alone and not to",
    "ECP-R3's surface.",
    "",
    "⭐ AP-16 CHECK, PERFORMED AND RECORDED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. §9.1's row for this id reads \"Envelope",
    "structure with per-entity hash validation (§3.1)\" — a POINTER that summarizes and cites the body it",
    "summarizes, not an independent restatement. Body and row AGREE, and the row asserts nothing the body",
    "does not. ⛔ This check is not optional bookkeeping: ECP-R57 was authored from a §9.1 row that",
    "CONTRADICTED §4.6 and §5.2a, the transcription was faithful, and our instrument scored 34 of 37",
    "peers against it (F75). Verified further: §9.1 is byte-identical .24 -> .25 except for ONE row, and",
    "that row is ECP-R57's, not this one's.",
    "",
    "⭐ THE CODE IS PINNED, AND .25 NARROWS THE PIN RATHER THAN MOVING IT. §5.2a corollary 1 pinned",
    "`400 hash_mismatch` at .24. At .25 the corollary gains a scoping warning in its own words:",
    "",
    "  \"⚠ The code above is THIS arm's, not the class's [MUST] (0.8.2.25). `400 hash_mismatch` answers a",
    "  **resolution-integrity** refusal — an `included` key that does not bind to its entity. It is the",
    "  wrong answer for bytes that were never hashed: a frame that does not decode into an Envelope at",
    "  all is `400 invalid_request` (§4.7, §4.11).\"",
    "",
    "⇒ The pin still reaches THIS probe and is now narrower around it. §4.11's cause table states the",
    "same binding as a row: \"Resolution integrity — an `included` entry whose key is not",
    "`content_hash({type, data})` of the entity under it -> 400 hash_mismatch, stated at §5.2a.\"",
    "",
    "THE PROBE'S ENTRY IS \"MIS-KEYED\" BY THE SPECIFICATION'S OWN DEFINITION, so the pin reaches it.",
    "§1.8 item 1 mechanism (a) defines the condition: \"reject any entry whose key is not",
    "`content_hash({type, data})` of the entity under it\". The probe's key equals the entity's CARRIED",
    "content_hash and both equal the hash of the entity's ORIGINAL data; the data was then changed. So",
    "`content_hash({type, data})` of what arrives is equal to neither. That is the named condition.",
    "",
    "⭐⭐ AND THE §1.8 MECHANISM-(b) CARVE-OUT DOES NOT REACH THIS FILE — CHECKED, BECAUSE A COUNTERPART",
    "GAVE US THE WARNING FOR FREE. §1.8 item 1 admits two mechanisms and a peer MUST implement at least",
    "one: (a) bind the key, or (b) \"discard the key — drop wire-supplied keys at the decode boundary and",
    "address entities exclusively by a `content_hash` validated under this item\". §5.2a: a mechanism-(b)",
    "peer never DETECTS a mis-key — the lookup misses, and a miss inherits the row of the step that",
    "missed — so \"a uniform verdict across all three rows MUST NOT be required\". ⇒ That carve-out is",
    "about the KEY. THIS PROBE'S DEFECT IS SELF-CONSISTENCY: the entity's own carried `content_hash` does",
    "not match its own {type, data}, which is §1.8 item 1's FIRST half and which mechanism (b)",
    "\"depends on ... running at EVERY ingress\" — in the spec's own words, without it \"a peer that skips",
    "the validation pass has re-created the defect one level down\". So a mechanism-(b) peer detects this",
    "probe by the validation it is REQUIRED to run. ⛔ The carve-out lands on ECP-R7-pending-b, whose",
    "surface IS the key, and that file's arms have NOT yet been re-read against it (K-MECH, owed).",
    "",
    "AND ONE CODE IS EXPLICITLY NON-CONFORMANT, which is the scoreable half (0.8.2.24, restated at",
    "§4.11 for the adjacent framing arm at .25):",
    "",
    "  \"`400 non_canonical_ecf` is NOT conformant here [MUST]: ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §5.4 defines that",
    "  code for CBOR tag-policy violations — any CBOR major-type-6 item in a data-field position — and a",
    "  mis-keyed `included` entry carries no tag. Its encoding is canonical; what is false is the claim",
    "  the key makes, and the remedy the code selects (re-encode) sends an honest caller to the wrong",
    "  layer.\"",
    "",
    "Checked against the encoding document rather than taken on the cross-reference: ECF 1.7 §5.4",
    "decoding paragraph scopes the code to tags and nothing else. The probe's frame carries no tag.",
    "⭐ §4.11 generalizes the principle in one sentence worth keeping: \"the code selects the caller's",
    "remedy, so a code that is merely in the right family is still wrong.\"",
    "",
    "§4.7 DOES NOT GOVERN THIS, AND THAT WAS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. §4.7 is the authoritative",
    "(status, code) registry for CONNECTION-HANDSHAKE failures and says so, adding that §5.2a \"MUST NOT be",
    "read as independent registries\". Its ten rows are negotiation, the three §4.6 proof-of-possession",
    "steps, ingest dispatch, already-established, out-of-order and unknown-operation. **None of them is a",
    "mis-keyed included entity**, and the refusal is placed \"before the envelope becomes a request\" —",
    "earlier than any §4.6 step. The probe is a hello only because a hello needs no author, no capability",
    "and no grant, which keeps the refusal attributable to the corrupted entity and to no posture.",
    "",
    "⛔⭐ WHAT .25 CHANGED, AND IT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS FILE WAS RE-AUTHORED. The .24 text of this",
    "reading said a close and a silence are \"recorded as `inconclusive_pending_ruling`, never scored\",",
    "because CQ-34 and CQ-35 owned them. BOTH ARE RULED, folded as §4.11:",
    "",
    "  \"A peer that refuses a frame pre-admission MUST put a coded EXECUTE_RESPONSE on the wire [MUST] —",
    "  correlated by `request_id` where the id is available, and otherwise as a best-effort coded frame",
    "  carrying no correlation. Whether the peer closes the connection afterwards is its own choice.\"",
    "",
    "  \"Two behaviours are non-conformant, and they are distinct failures rather than one\" — dropping the",
    "  frame (\"the caller learns nothing until its own §6.11(c) deadline expires, and the refusal is",
    "  unobservable to every instrument\") and closing with no coded frame (\"indistinguishable from a",
    "  network fault (§4.6) ... and the two remedies are opposite\").",
    "",
    "⇒ THEY ARE SCORED, AND SCORED SEPARATELY. A suite that collapses them lets a peer get credit for the",
    "wrong fix. ⇒ And the close is NO LONGER EVIDENCE OF ANYTHING on its own: a peer that closes after",
    "emitting the coded frame is conformant; one that closes without it is not.",
    "",
    "STATE. The subject is a HELLO — a pre-handshake frame — which is deliberate and unchanged: it needs",
    "no author, no capability and no grant, so the refusal is attributable to the corrupted entity and to",
    "no posture. §4.11 reaches it because a pre-admission refusal is defined by the frame not yet being",
    "an admitted request, which is true of a hello by construction."
  ],
  "scope_correction": [
    "⛔⛔ RE-SCOPED 2026-09-16, THE SAME DAY IT WAS RE-AUTHORED AND RUN — AND THE RULING PREDATES THE RUN.",
    "",
    "0.8.2.26 §1.8 item 1 added, and it lands directly on this file's probe:",
    "",
    "  \"A uniform verdict on an UNREFERENCED `included` entry is mechanism-shaped and MUST NOT be",
    "  required [MUST] (0.8.2.26). Mechanism (a) inspects every entry as the map is accepted, so an",
    "  unreferenced mis-keyed entry is refused; mechanism (b) has no wire key to inspect and no entry to",
    "  reach, so the same input is NOT REPRESENTED AT ALL in the peer's decoded form. Both are",
    "  conformant, and the observable difference is a property of the mechanism rather than of the",
    "  peer's correctness. A conformance check MUST NOT assert a refusal on this input: asserting one",
    "  votes mechanism (a) and makes (b) — which this item blesses — unimplementable.\"",
    "",
    "⛔ THIS FILE'S PROBE IS THAT INPUT, BY DESIGN. Its own reading says so in terms: 'the probe includes",
    "an entity the hello has no use for'. Being unreferenced was the POINT — it was how we reached §3.1's",
    "'each' rather than the weaker 'each one the handler uses'. 0.8.2.26 rules that the observable",
    "difference on that input is a property of the MECHANISM, not of the peer's correctness.",
    "",
    "⇒ THE 2026-09-16 RUN'S FOUR FAIL VERDICTS ARE NOT SCOREABLE AND ARE DEMOTED TO WITNESSES. They were",
    "held unrouted pending a wider census, which is the only reason the damage is zero — the same",
    "restraint that saved F75's 34 peers.",
    "",
    "⚠ AND THE TIMING IS THE FINDING RATHER THAN THE ERROR. 0.8.2.26 landed at 09:25 and the run was",
    "taken at ~11:45. THE RULING EXISTED BEFORE THE MEASUREMENT and nobody here had read it, because",
    "arch's packet was not enumerated — AP-17 a third time in two days. The re-authoring was correct",
    "against the snapshot it declared and wrong about the world. ⇒ READ THE INBOX BEFORE AUTHORING.",
    "",
    "WHAT SURVIVES, STATED PRECISELY. The OBSERVATION stands and is real cohort data: three generator",
    "peers answer `400 non_canonical_ecf` and core-go bare-closes on a self-inconsistent included entity.",
    "What does NOT survive is SCORING it — on an unreferenced entry this file may not require any refusal",
    "at all, so neither the code nor the frame obligation is assertable there.",
    "",
    "THE RE-SCOPE ARCH ASKED FOR ('re-scope rather than re-score'): the obligation is restated over a",
    "REFERENCED entry — one the peer must resolve to do its job — where BOTH mechanisms must reach it.",
    "Mechanism (b) addresses entities by a content_hash validated under item 1's first half, so a",
    "referenced self-inconsistent entity fails for it exactly as for mechanism (a). ⬜ THE PROBE FOR THAT",
    "IS NOT BUILT, AND IT IS NOT A RENAME OF THE CURRENT ONE: a hello's `included` map may carry no entry",
    "the peer is OBLIGED to resolve, so the referenced surface may need an authenticated EXECUTE rather",
    "than a hello — which reintroduces the posture confound the hello was chosen to avoid. A real design",
    "question, left open rather than guessed at."
  ],
